{
  "surface": "packages/plugin-api/view.js#createViewBridge calls",
  "description": "Ordered steps of the tab calls of a view page. Each case sends a tab call through the call layer of the bridge with the parameters that the call takes (docs/spec/native-surfaces.md, view calls: tab.title, tab.footer, tab.directory, tab.modified and tab.error take the value; tab.notify takes the notice fields {kind, title, text, action, system} and replies the notice id, tab.progress takes {id, progress}, tab.done takes {id, kind, title}; tab.keep takes {reason, on}). The page calls page.notify, page.progress and page.done take the same fields and reply the same as tab.notify, tab.progress and tab.done (docs/spec/native-surfaces.md, view calls). The first step sends a valid value, and the host answers its reply (null, or the notice id for tab.notify). The second step sends an invalid value, and the host answers with the refusal of the workbench for that value (its text is the one the tab reports refuse with). The cases verify the request that the bridge posts and that the reply and the refusal of the host reach the view unchanged: the bridge validates no tab value itself. Each step lists the posted call, the result and the error text.",
